Z||000000||88formula||10-24-1999||03:05 PM||||Has anyone here ever put 215/60R14's on an 87 pontiac fiero coupe all the way around the car? What does this do to the steering effort? The car originally came with 195/70R14's on all four wheels. Any advice would be appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||10-24-1999||04:49 PM||||My 85 GT had a set of 215-60-14 tires on it when I bought it. Nothing wrong with that size tire on a Fiero. I thought it handled nice. All kinds of room under the wheel wells with that size tire.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||10-24-1999||05:49 PM||||Thanks for the info. I'm going to try it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||10-25-1999||09:04 AM||||I have a matched set of 215/60/14s and the car steers fine.  Rides nice too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87FieroGT||10-26-1999||11:54 PM||||I have a matched set of Centenial 245/45/ ZR 16's on Konig Rush rims on my 87 Fiero GT. Looks good and rides like a dream.||||reg||1
